---
import CalcPage from '../../components/CalcPage.astro';
import Field from '../../components/Field.astro';
---

<CalcPage
  title="BSA and BSA-based dosing"
  kicker="Dosing"
  lede="Mosteller turns height and weight into body surface area. Once you have BSA in m², an order written in mg/m² becomes an ordinary multiply, and 1.73 m² is the adult figure those orders are often referenced against."
  description="Calculate Mosteller body surface area from height and weight, convert lb and inches along the way, and turn mg/m² orders into patient doses using the 1.73 m² adult reference."
>
  <form slot="form" id="calc">
    <input type="hidden" name="mode" value="bsa" />

    <div class="modes" role="group" aria-label="Choose what to solve for">
      <button class="mode-btn" type="button" data-mode="bsa" aria-pressed="true">
        Find BSA
      </button>
      <button class="mode-btn" type="button" data-mode="dose" aria-pressed="false">
        Dose from mg/m²
      </button>
      <button class="mode-btn" type="button" data-mode="perM2" aria-pressed="false">
        Find mg/m²
      </button>
    </div>

    <fieldset>
      <legend>Patient size</legend>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <Field
          label="BSA (m²)"
          name="bsa"
          placeholder="optional for dosing modes"
          hint="Used only when finding a dose or mg/m². Leave blank to calculate Mosteller from height and weight. Ignored when you are only finding BSA."
        />
      </div>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <Field label="Height" name="height" placeholder="70" />
        <div class="field">
          <label for="heightUnit">Height unit</label>
          <select id="heightUnit" name="heightUnit">
            <option value="in" selected>Inches (in)</option>
            <option value="cm">Centimeters (cm)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <Field label="Weight" name="weight" placeholder="150" />
        <div class="field">
          <label for="weightUnit">Weight unit</label>
          <select id="weightUnit" name="weightUnit">
            <option value="lb" selected>Pounds (lb)</option>
            <option value="kg">Kilograms (kg)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-top:-0.6rem">
        Conversions used here: 1 in = 2.54 cm, and 2.2 lb = 1 kg. Feet are left
        out on purpose; convert to inches first if that is what you were given.
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <div data-mode-panel="bsa">
      <div class="field-actions">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Find BSA</button>
        <button class="btn btn--quiet" type="reset">Clear</button>
      </div>
      <div class="field-actions" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
        <button
          class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
          type="button"
          data-example='{"mode":"bsa","bsa":"","height":"70","heightUnit":"in","weight":"150","weightUnit":"lb"}'
        >
          Example: 70 in, 150 lb
        </button>
        <button
          class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
          type="button"
          data-example='{"mode":"bsa","bsa":"","height":"170","heightUnit":"cm","weight":"70","weightUnit":"kg"}'
        >
          Example: 170 cm, 70 kg
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div data-mode-panel="dose" hidden>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>The order</legend>
        <div class="field-grid">
          <Field
            label="Ordered dose (mg/m²)"
            name="ordered"
            placeholder="75"
            hint="The protocol dose, written per square meter of BSA."
          />
        </div>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="field-actions">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Find the dose</button>
        <button class="btn btn--quiet" type="reset">Clear</button>
      </div>
      <div class="field-actions" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
        <button
          class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
          type="button"
          data-example='{"mode":"dose","ordered":"75","bsa":"1.73","height":"","weight":"","heightUnit":"in","weightUnit":"lb"}'
        >
          Example: 75 mg/m² for a 1.73 m² adult
        </button>
        <button
          class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
          type="button"
          data-example='{"mode":"dose","ordered":"75","bsa":"","height":"70","heightUnit":"in","weight":"150","weightUnit":"lb"}'
        >
          Example: 75 mg/m², 70 in / 150 lb
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div data-mode-panel="perM2" hidden>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>What was given</legend>
        <div class="field-grid">
          <Field
            label="Total dose (mg)"
            name="totalDose"
            placeholder="130"
            hint="The milligram amount the patient actually received, or the amount you are checking against the protocol."
          />
        </div>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="field-actions">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Find mg/m²</button>
        <button class="btn btn--quiet" type="reset">Clear</button>
      </div>
      <div class="field-actions" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
        <button
          class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
          type="button"
          data-example='{"mode":"perM2","totalDose":"130","bsa":"1.73","height":"","weight":"","heightUnit":"in","weightUnit":"lb"}'
        >
          Example: 130 mg on a 1.73 m² adult
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>

  <div slot="concept">
    <h2>Surface area, not just weight</h2>
    <p>
      Some drugs are ordered per square meter of body surface area because that
      tracks better with how the body clears them than weight alone. The number
      you need first is BSA in m².
    </p>

    <h3>Mosteller</h3>
    <pre class="formula">BSA (m²) = √( (height(cm) × weight(kg)) / 3600 )</pre>
    <p>
      Height has to be in centimeters and weight in kilograms before the
      formula sees them. The conversions this calculator uses on purpose are
      the same ones the rest of the site teaches:
    </p>
    <pre class="formula">1 in  =  2.54 cm
2.2 lb  =  1 kg</pre>

    <h3>Turning mg/m² into a dose</h3>
    <pre class="formula">patient dose (mg)  =  ordered (mg/m²)  ×  BSA (m²)</pre>
    <p>
      The square meters cancel. What you are left with is a plain milligram
      amount for that patient.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>The 1.73 m² reference.</strong> Many adult protocols and
        textbook examples are written as if the patient has 1.73 m² of surface
        area. It is a conventional average adult figure, not a measurement of
        the person in front of you. Use the patient's own BSA for the actual
        dose; keep 1.73 around as the reference the order was sized against.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</CalcPage>

<script>
  import { setupCalculator, setupModes } from '../../scripts/calc.js';
  import { solveBsa } from '../../scripts/solvers/bsa.js';

  const modeInput = document.querySelector('input[name="mode"]');

  const calc = setupCalculator({
    form: '#calc',
    onPreset(preset) {
      if (preset.mode) activate(preset.mode);
    },
    solve: solveBsa,
  });

  const activate = setupModes((mode) => {
    modeInput.value = mode;
    calc.clear();
  });
</script>
